WEBVTT

00:12.851 --> 00:15.217
Ah. Oh! Oh, oh.

00:15.387 --> 00:18.356
Oh, hot, hot, hot. Oh, God.

00:19.825 --> 00:21.122
Oh, God.

00:21.293 --> 00:24.524
Oh, God. Oh, God.

00:28.934 --> 00:30.902
Oh, God, oh.

00:31.069 --> 00:33.765
Oh, God, oh, God.

00:33.939 --> 00:35.770
Oh, God.

00:35.941 --> 00:39.206
I was picturing something
entirely different.

00:40.278 --> 00:41.472
I couldn't sleep.

00:41.646 --> 00:45.104
So you decided
to make your nipples hard?

00:45.584 --> 00:49.645
Oh, the peas.
No, I was heating up some milk and...

00:49.821 --> 00:51.152
You know, my nipple is hard.

00:52.324 --> 00:54.656
If you can't sleep,
why don't you just take a pill?

00:54.826 --> 00:56.521
I don't believe in pills.

00:56.695 --> 01:00.961
- What about booze? Believe in booze?
- That's not sleeping, that's passing out.

01:01.533 --> 01:03.558
Potato, potato.

01:03.735 --> 01:06.533
I have a lot on my mind.
I don't need to drug myself.

01:06.705 --> 01:09.970
Okay, well, in that case,
I do know a great all-natural sleep aid.

01:10.542 --> 01:13.340
- What's that?
- Sex, you should get yourself some sex.

01:13.512 --> 01:14.604
It'll put you right out.

01:15.013 --> 01:16.071
- Charlie.
- Look at me.

01:16.248 --> 01:18.273
I can hardly keep my eyes open.

01:18.450 --> 01:20.611
No, sex is not really an option
at the moment.

01:20.786 --> 01:22.754
You telling me you can't make a fist?

01:22.921 --> 01:24.320
Just leave me alone.

01:25.791 --> 01:27.019
How about exercise?

01:27.192 --> 01:29.319
It's kind of like sex
but without the condom.

01:30.295 --> 01:31.762
You know, that's not a bad idea.

01:31.930 --> 01:34.865
Well, you should always wear a condom.

01:35.033 --> 01:38.264
No, I mean the exercise.
I could go for a run on the beach.

01:38.436 --> 01:39.903
Sure, I've seen people do that.

01:40.071 --> 01:42.869
Usually they have a dog,
but I think that's optional.

01:43.041 --> 01:44.633
Actually, that's a great idea.

01:44.810 --> 01:47.108
I don't know where
you're gonna get a dog.

01:47.279 --> 01:48.974
You really enjoy screwing with me?

01:49.447 --> 01:52.314
Well, you don't pay rent.

01:52.684 --> 01:55.949
- You know what? I'm gonna do it.
- Pay rent?

01:56.888 --> 01:58.651
No.

01:58.824 --> 02:00.519
I'm gonna jog to the pier and back.

02:00.926 --> 02:03.656
Maybe I can burn off my excess energy.

02:04.696 --> 02:06.459
Attaboy.

02:16.775 --> 02:19.573
No, I prefer the Tater Tots.

02:24.983 --> 02:27.110
This will do it.

02:27.285 --> 02:29.480
Burn off that energy.

02:36.828 --> 02:38.853
That's interesting.

03:04.089 --> 03:06.080
Nice night for a run.

03:06.491 --> 03:08.425
How rude.

03:09.895 --> 03:12.022
&lt;i>MAN
This is the Los Angeles Sheriff's Department.&lt;/i>

03:12.197 --> 03:14.529
&lt;i>Stop running and drop to the ground
with your arms spread.&lt;/i>

03:14.699 --> 03:16.963
Oh, no, no, no.
You've got the wrong guy.

03:17.135 --> 03:20.070
&lt;i>- The guy you want ran that way.
- This is your last warning.&lt;/i>

03:20.238 --> 03:22.263
&lt;i>Drop to the ground
with your arms spread.&lt;/i>

03:22.440 --> 03:24.601
No, you don't understand.

03:24.776 --> 03:26.767
Follow me, I'll show you.

03:34.886 --> 03:38.219
&lt;i>Put your hands behind your head
and drop to your knees.&lt;/i>

03:38.890 --> 03:40.585
No, no, you don't understand.

03:40.759 --> 03:42.226
I just couldn't sleep.

03:42.394 --> 03:44.225
&lt;i>Release the dogs.&lt;/i>

03:44.896 --> 03:47.660
Dogs? No.

03:47.832 --> 03:48.992
No, no dogs.

04:14.726 --> 04:17.923
All right, all right, I'm coming.

04:19.731 --> 04:21.790
This better be good.

04:26.538 --> 04:29.029
Hey, it is good.

04:29.474 --> 04:30.907
Charlie, tell them who I am.

04:31.076 --> 04:33.442
I'm sorry, who are you?

04:33.611 --> 04:36.603
Charlie, if you don't tell them,
they're gonna take me to jail.

04:36.781 --> 04:39.215
Why do you keep calling me Charlie?

04:39.718 --> 04:42.084
Sir, is this man living here or not?

04:42.253 --> 04:44.118
Define living.

04:44.289 --> 04:47.918
- Charlie, I swear on my sors life...
- Yeah, he lives here.

04:48.760 --> 04:50.625
Told you. I have got your badge numbers.

04:50.795 --> 04:53.423
- I am gonna write a scathing letter to the...
- Shut up.

04:53.598 --> 04:56.499
Thank you, officers.
You are a credit to the Malibu community.

04:56.668 --> 04:57.760
You have a nice evening.

04:57.936 --> 05:01.167
At least this clown didn't ask
if I was Jewish.

05:06.644 --> 05:08.305
So...

05:08.480 --> 05:10.243
...how was your run?

05:35.840 --> 05:38.206
Enough drumming.

05:39.377 --> 05:42.574
Fine. Bass solo.

05:44.816 --> 05:45.840
Oh, come on.

05:46.017 --> 05:47.780
I'd like to have a nice quiet dinner.

05:47.952 --> 05:51.752
And I'd like you to be a keno waitress
who can fit her entire hand in her mouth...

05:51.923 --> 05:53.481
...but here you sit.

05:54.459 --> 05:57.553
I'm sorry, I'm a little cranky.
I haven't slept in two days.

05:57.729 --> 05:59.594
Why don't you take a pill?

06:00.698 --> 06:02.188
He doesn't believe in pills.

06:02.367 --> 06:05.359
How can you not believe in them?
They're on Tv all the time.

06:07.138 --> 06:08.332
Let me tell you something.

06:08.506 --> 06:11.407
Big companies want you to think
you can take a pill for everything.

06:11.576 --> 06:14.170
Can't sleep? Take a pill.
Can't wake up? Take a pill.

06:14.345 --> 06:17.371
Feeling sad? Take a pill.
Can't get it up? Take a pill.

06:17.549 --> 06:19.574
Can't get what up?

06:23.721 --> 06:25.245
Can we just eat our dinner?

06:29.094 --> 06:31.028
Can I go back to Mom's tomorrow?

06:31.196 --> 06:33.357
- Why?
- I wanna hang out with my friends.

06:33.531 --> 06:35.328
All of a sudden your father's
not good enough?

06:35.967 --> 06:38.561
It's not all of a sudden.

06:40.672 --> 06:43.573
Come on, Alan, the kid's growing up.
He's got his own life now.

06:43.741 --> 06:45.902
How about you have your friends
come over here?

06:46.077 --> 06:48.238
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

06:48.413 --> 06:50.847
- No kids in my house.
- I'm a kid.

06:51.783 --> 06:55.651
Well, I don't... I don't think of you as a kid.
I think of you as more of...

06:55.820 --> 06:57.845
...a gassy dwarf.

06:59.858 --> 07:02.122
Charlie, you said it yourself.

07:02.293 --> 07:05.228
He's growing up.
Getting a life of his own.

07:05.396 --> 07:07.330
He'll be going off to college soon.

07:07.499 --> 07:09.194
I'll only see him on holidays.

07:09.367 --> 07:11.198
Only hear from him
when he needs money.

07:11.369 --> 07:16.033
Not that I'll have any.
I'll still be paying alimony to two ex-wives.

07:16.207 --> 07:20.871
And college tuition? That just means
selling an organ or turning tricks.

07:22.280 --> 07:23.770
And for what?

07:23.948 --> 07:26.178
So that he can get
a won'thless piece of paper...

07:26.351 --> 07:29.411
...that he can then fold into a hat
to wear to the fast-food job...

07:29.587 --> 07:33.546
...that he will probably be fired from
for stealing fries from the customers' bags.

07:39.097 --> 07:41.088
I do like fries.

07:53.611 --> 07:55.909
Sure, you can sleep.

07:56.414 --> 07:58.109
You have no conscience.

08:00.018 --> 08:01.713
Wake up!

08:05.690 --> 08:08.022
- What?
- It's noon.

08:08.193 --> 08:09.888
What day?

08:10.261 --> 08:11.285
Saturday.

08:11.462 --> 08:13.623
Thanks, see you Sunday.

08:14.299 --> 08:15.857
Charlie, I have to go out.

08:16.034 --> 08:18.002
I need you to watch Jake and his friend.

08:18.169 --> 08:20.933
Friend? I thought I said no kids.

08:21.105 --> 08:22.265
You say lots of stuff.

08:22.440 --> 08:25.432
Twice a week you say
you'll never drink again.

08:25.610 --> 08:28.101
I don't know what to believe anymore.

08:28.613 --> 08:29.807
Where are you going?

08:29.981 --> 08:31.346
I have to run some errands.

08:31.516 --> 08:33.211
- So take the kids with you.
- I can't.

08:33.384 --> 08:35.284
- Run errands later.
- Would you please...

08:35.453 --> 08:37.216
...get your drunken ass out of bed...

08:37.388 --> 08:41.757
...and stop being a waste of skin
for once in your life!

08:44.329 --> 08:46.126
Well, since you said "please. "

08:47.865 --> 08:49.389
Thank you.

08:51.569 --> 08:53.332
I'm... I'm sorry I barked at you.

08:53.771 --> 08:56.137
- Still can't sleep, huh?
- No.

08:56.608 --> 08:59.668
Well, don't worry, I'm here for you.
I'll keep an eye on the kids.

08:59.844 --> 09:02.335
- I appreciate it.
- No problem.

09:09.587 --> 09:13.887
It's like he's never met me.

09:17.362 --> 09:18.556
Nothing seems to work.

09:18.730 --> 09:23.394
I've tried warm milk, exercise,
meditation, self-hypnosis...

09:23.568 --> 09:25.331
Why don't you just take a pill?

09:26.671 --> 09:30.402
Because I don't need a pill.
The root of my insomnia is psychological.

09:30.575 --> 09:33.066
That is why I'm sitting here with you,
a psychologist.

09:33.244 --> 09:38.238
I'm a psychiatrist, a medical doctor,
which is why I can prescribe pills.

09:38.416 --> 09:41.044
Is that a shot at me
because I'm just a chiropractor?

09:41.219 --> 09:44.746
No, of course not. But I am a real doctor.

09:45.890 --> 09:47.414
Look, can you help me or not?

09:47.592 --> 09:51.187
You know, delve into my subconscious,
unravel the source of my problem?

09:51.362 --> 09:53.387
Sure, I'll give it a shot.

09:54.165 --> 09:56.133
So when was the last time you had sex?

09:56.301 --> 09:58.496
This has nothing to do with sex.

09:58.670 --> 10:01.935
This has to do with alimony
and ex-wives and child support...

10:02.106 --> 10:05.564
...and writing checks I can't cover and
having to live on my brother's hide-a-bed.

10:05.743 --> 10:09.076
- Why don't we start with your brother?
- What does he have to do with this?

10:09.247 --> 10:11.715
- Who's the doctor here?
- Okay, that was a shot.

10:12.317 --> 10:13.807
You got me.

10:15.486 --> 10:17.044
Now tell me about your brother.

10:18.323 --> 10:19.813
What is there to say?

10:19.991 --> 10:23.518
He's two years older than me,
but much more immature.

10:23.695 --> 10:26.664
He's charming and easy-going,
of course, why shouldn't he be?

10:26.831 --> 10:29.356
He's never had to work for anything
in his entire life.

10:29.534 --> 10:34.562
Money and women just seem to fall
into his big, fat, lucky lap.

10:35.206 --> 10:36.605
So you resent him.

10:36.774 --> 10:39.572
No, I love him. He took me in
when I needed a place to live.

10:39.744 --> 10:43.145
Okay, you say you love your brother,
you're grateful for his help...

10:43.314 --> 10:46.374
...and yet it must be difficult
to watch him sail through life...

10:46.551 --> 10:50.578
...while you remain a complete
and utter failure.

10:52.757 --> 10:54.816
I didn't say I was a complete failure.

10:54.992 --> 10:56.186
Huh.

10:56.361 --> 10:58.659
Why is it in my notes?

10:59.364 --> 11:01.423
Oh, well, continue.

11:01.966 --> 11:03.957
Okay.

11:04.235 --> 11:09.002
Well, the worst part is that as selfish
and promiscuous as Charlie is...

11:09.173 --> 11:11.437
...he hasn't suffered any consequences.

11:11.609 --> 11:16.205
No palimony suits,
no bullet wounds from angry husbands.

11:16.381 --> 11:20.010
Not so much
as a lousy urinary tract infection.

11:20.184 --> 11:22.880
- And yet you love him.
- Well, he's family.

11:25.223 --> 11:27.817
Oh, oh, I get it.

11:27.992 --> 11:32.053
You think it's this internal contradiction
that's the source of my insomnia.

11:32.230 --> 11:33.322
What do you think?

11:33.965 --> 11:35.899
I think you may be right.

11:36.067 --> 11:37.364
But how do I resolve it?

11:37.535 --> 11:40.629
Well, that's a good question.
But unfortunately, we're out of time.

11:41.105 --> 11:44.541
- Already?
- You dozed off for 40 minutes, Alan.

11:44.709 --> 11:48.338
- You're gonna charge me for that?
- I was awake.

11:50.648 --> 11:52.309
Fine, fine. Can I write you a check?

11:52.483 --> 11:53.882
Oh, boy.

11:54.051 --> 11:57.384
Alan, when a patient tells me
they're writing checks they can't cover...

11:57.555 --> 12:00.649
...I kind of have a little cash-only policy.

12:01.726 --> 12:04.320
All right. Where's the closest ATM?

12:04.495 --> 12:05.587
Downstairs in the lobby.

12:05.763 --> 12:08.527
- I'll be right back.
- I'll walk with you.

12:31.923 --> 12:33.413
Hey.

12:33.591 --> 12:35.525
- What you doing?
- Chatting.

12:35.693 --> 12:37.558
- With who?
- Each other.

12:37.728 --> 12:39.218
But you're in the same room.

12:44.202 --> 12:45.965
What are you typing? Is that about me?

12:47.238 --> 12:48.728
No.

12:50.408 --> 12:51.739
Down the hall, on the right.

12:51.909 --> 12:53.274
BRB.

12:57.215 --> 12:59.979
- "BRB"?
- Be right back.

13:00.151 --> 13:01.618
Ah.

13:01.786 --> 13:04.721
Well, YAD.

13:04.889 --> 13:07.790
- What's that?
- You're a dog.

13:10.261 --> 13:13.094
- She's cute.
- She's just a friend.

13:16.934 --> 13:18.629
- What are you doing?
- Oh, come on.

13:18.803 --> 13:20.031
It's me you're talking to.

13:20.204 --> 13:21.796
The big dog.

13:23.975 --> 13:26.273
Okay, okay, you're starting
to freak me out.

13:27.945 --> 13:29.537
TAYLoR:
That's my mom.

13:29.714 --> 13:31.648
- I'll get it.
- Okay, okay, I lied.

13:31.816 --> 13:33.181
I like her.

13:33.351 --> 13:36.809
- Oh, really?
- Yeah. Woof.

13:38.055 --> 13:39.079
There you go.

13:39.857 --> 13:41.256
Wait, don't open the door.

13:41.959 --> 13:44.052
- Why not?
- Coming.

13:44.228 --> 13:46.093
Go to your room.

13:46.264 --> 13:48.824
- What are you, nuts?
- Please don't hit on her.

13:49.000 --> 13:51.161
- Hit on who?
- Taylor's mom.

13:51.335 --> 13:53.030
Why would I hit on Taylor's mom?

13:53.204 --> 13:57.197
Well, because she's kind of pretty
and you'll hit on anything with a pulse.

13:58.209 --> 14:00.268
- Where'd you get that?
- My mom.

14:00.444 --> 14:04.039
- Oh, well...
- And my dad, Berta, Rose, Grandma...

14:04.215 --> 14:06.376
- okay, okay.
... the UPS man.

14:06.551 --> 14:07.745
All right.

14:07.919 --> 14:10.854
And when you hit on people I know,
everything gets screwed up...

14:11.022 --> 14:13.923
...or I have to find
a new guitar teacher, new karate class...

14:14.091 --> 14:15.956
...Cub Scout troop...
- okay, I get it.

14:16.127 --> 14:17.788
- Godmother.

14:17.962 --> 14:21.796
You don't have to worry. I'm not gonna risk
our friendship over "kind of pretty. "

14:21.966 --> 14:25.458
- So you won't hit on her?
- Absolutely not.

14:27.204 --> 14:29.138
Hi, I'm Taylor's mom.

14:31.676 --> 14:33.337
Scratch that.

14:37.214 --> 14:40.581
- Okay, I will give you a call.
- Great. Bye.

14:47.592 --> 14:49.025
You promised.

14:49.193 --> 14:50.524
No, no. No.

14:50.695 --> 14:54.028
The head that made the promise
is not the one that broke it.

14:56.601 --> 14:59.297
And besides,
you said she was just kind of pretty.

14:59.470 --> 15:02.200
- Who do you consider hot?
- Taylor.

15:02.373 --> 15:05.672
- Taylor's 12.
- Hello.

15:06.210 --> 15:08.610
Come on. What's the worst thing
that could happen...

15:08.779 --> 15:12.215
...if I go out with your friend's mom?
- Do I have to explain it again?

15:12.383 --> 15:15.409
- My guitar teacher, my karate coach...
- okay, okay.

15:15.586 --> 15:18.555
I can't show my face
at the comic-book store.

15:18.889 --> 15:21.881
All right, but the worst thing
doesn't have to happen.

15:22.059 --> 15:24.653
Would you please
just not go out with her?

15:26.497 --> 15:28.226
Tell you what, I'll make you a deal.

15:28.399 --> 15:31.334
I'll give up Taylor's mom
in exchange for you washing my car...

15:31.502 --> 15:33.129
...once a week for a month.
- Done.

15:33.304 --> 15:36.398
That includes Turtle Wax,
tire dressing and vacuuming the carpets.

15:36.574 --> 15:38.701
- Oh, man.
- Hey, the woman is recently divorced.

15:38.876 --> 15:41.003
I didn't ask for her number,
she gave it to me.

15:41.178 --> 15:42.611
- You know what that means?
- No.

15:42.780 --> 15:45.874
That means one,
maybe two dinners and...

15:48.352 --> 15:49.444
You're waxing my car.

15:50.488 --> 15:52.251
All right.

15:52.757 --> 15:55.317
You're lucky
you're not painting the house.

15:56.027 --> 15:58.655
The sacrifices we make for our kids.

15:59.797 --> 16:02.595
- Hey.
- Hey.

16:03.200 --> 16:04.690
You look like crap.

16:04.869 --> 16:08.066
- Thank you. You look terrific.
- I feel terrific.

16:08.239 --> 16:10.002
The key is a good night's sleep.

16:10.541 --> 16:13.476
Yeah, listen, I have to talk to you.

16:13.644 --> 16:15.635
- This is a bad time, Alan.
- How come?

16:15.813 --> 16:17.280
Because you wanna talk to me.

16:19.283 --> 16:20.841
Okay, what?

16:21.252 --> 16:23.015
You know I love you, right?

16:23.187 --> 16:25.621
Alan, are you breaking up with me?

16:26.123 --> 16:30.321
- Would you just shut up and listen to me?
- Pick one, Alan.

16:31.262 --> 16:34.459
All right, all right.
I talked to a therapist...

16:36.400 --> 16:38.561
...and I think I learned something.

16:39.036 --> 16:41.300
No, too easy. Go ahead.

16:41.706 --> 16:43.003
The thing is...

16:43.174 --> 16:46.302
...all these years of watching your life
go so smoothly...

16:46.477 --> 16:51.005
...while I stumble back and forth
between humiliation and abject failure...

16:51.182 --> 16:55.141
...has resulted in me harboring a lot
of anger and jealousy towards you.

16:55.319 --> 16:57.014
Yeah, I get that.

16:57.788 --> 16:59.312
How could it not?

17:00.291 --> 17:03.624
Anyway, I think the tension
between my love for you...

17:03.794 --> 17:06.490
...and my resentment of you
is what's causing my insomnia.

17:07.431 --> 17:08.762
- And?
- And I thought...

17:08.933 --> 17:11.731
...maybe if I got it out in the open,
it might help me sleep.

17:12.136 --> 17:13.603
So how do you feel now?

17:14.472 --> 17:15.734
Better, actually.

17:15.906 --> 17:18.431
Like... Like a weight has been lifted.

17:18.609 --> 17:20.440
- Well, good.
- Yeah, maybe that's it.

17:20.644 --> 17:22.509
Maybe all I needed to do was unload.

17:23.481 --> 17:26.848
Well, a good unloading
usually makes me drowsy.

17:27.017 --> 17:32.182
- You're disgusting.
- True, but I sleep like a baby.

17:32.356 --> 17:36.759
And if I wake up fussy, there's always
something nearby to put in my mouth.

17:59.083 --> 18:02.314
I waxed your car.

18:02.820 --> 18:04.879
What? What are you doing up?

18:05.055 --> 18:07.387
You were out with Taylor's mom,
werert you?

18:07.558 --> 18:09.958
- No, I wasrt.
- Are you sure?

18:10.127 --> 18:12.061
I think I know who I was out with.

18:12.229 --> 18:14.561
Okay, well, maybe
you can explain this picture...

18:14.732 --> 18:18.031
...of your perfectly waxed car
in Taylor's driveway.

18:19.603 --> 18:20.797
Where did you get that?

18:20.971 --> 18:23.735
Taylor took it with her phone
and e-mailed it to me.

18:23.908 --> 18:25.375
Oh, okay.

18:26.243 --> 18:28.074
Not my car.

18:28.879 --> 18:32.815
What about this one of you kissing
Taylor's mom in front of the car?

18:35.686 --> 18:36.983
Photoshop?

18:38.589 --> 18:39.817
How was your date?

18:40.057 --> 18:42.685
- Very nice.
- Bite me.

18:45.296 --> 18:46.627
Okay, well, good night.

18:46.797 --> 18:49.732
You said you wouldn't go out with her
and you did.

18:49.900 --> 18:52.130
I had to, Jake. She called me.

18:52.303 --> 18:53.793
What difference does that make?

18:53.971 --> 18:55.370
I have to explain it to you?

18:55.539 --> 18:57.973
I have to explain everything to you.

18:58.943 --> 19:02.572
Okay, okay. Let's say you're a hunter.

19:02.746 --> 19:06.375
If a deer takes your gun, shoots itself...

19:06.550 --> 19:09.678
...then straps itself
to the roof of your car...

19:10.087 --> 19:12.851
...you have to take it home and eat it.

19:14.091 --> 19:15.786
What?

19:16.260 --> 19:19.491
I'm sorry. I can't make it any clearer.

19:19.997 --> 19:22.625
If you keep seeing her,
you're gonna be sorry.

19:23.601 --> 19:25.466
Whoa, is that a threat?

19:25.636 --> 19:27.194
No, it's a promise.

19:27.371 --> 19:28.531
What's the difference?

19:28.706 --> 19:31.675
I don't know.
One's a threat and one's a promise.

19:34.311 --> 19:36.404
Oh, come on, buddy.
Let's be reasonable here.

19:36.580 --> 19:38.605
Your relationship with your friend
is what?

19:38.782 --> 19:41.478
Instant messaging and holding hands
at the pep rally?

19:41.652 --> 19:43.176
What's a pep rally?

19:43.354 --> 19:44.582
Just listen to me.

19:44.755 --> 19:47.485
Before you know it,
you'll have forgotten all about Taylor.

19:47.658 --> 19:49.319
You'll have forgotten her mother.

19:49.493 --> 19:51.222
No doubt.

19:51.395 --> 19:53.920
But I guarantee you
I'll be forgetting a lot more...

19:54.098 --> 19:55.998
...than holding her hand at a pep rally.

19:56.533 --> 19:58.000
Last chance, Uncle Charlie.

19:59.303 --> 20:02.101
Ooh. I'm so scared.

20:04.308 --> 20:08.039
"Last chance, Uncle Charlie. "
Pbbt. Please.

20:16.453 --> 20:18.683
Jake!

20:19.290 --> 20:21.349
- What's going on?
- Nothing. Gotta go.

20:21.892 --> 20:25.123
You're dead. You are so dead.

20:29.733 --> 20:31.132
Damn it.

20:40.477 --> 20:42.604
He went that way.

20:43.614 --> 20:45.241
Thanks.

20:46.850 --> 20:49.876
- Great slime.
- Thanks.

20:50.054 --> 20:52.249
It's an old family recipe.

20:53.891 --> 20:56.883
Where are you, you rat bastard?

20:57.061 --> 20:59.791
&lt;i>MAN
This is the Los Angeles Sheriff's Department.&lt;/i>

20:59.964 --> 21:02.091
&lt;i>Get down on the sand
with your arms spread.&lt;/i>

21:02.266 --> 21:03.494
It's okay.

21:03.667 --> 21:06.261
I'm just trying to kill a kid.

21:07.204 --> 21:09.672
&lt;i>Release the dogs.&lt;/i>

21:15.879 --> 21:17.471
That's right.

21:18.182 --> 21:21.015
Release the dogs.
